"text": "This might be the most important photo in startup history, and they are the reason the PayPal mafia might finally be getting some competition. It all starts with the kid next to Paul Graham. He built a location app with zero customers and still managed to sell it for $43 million. Sam went from a $6,000 check in YC to building OpenAI and raising $122 billion, the largest private round in history. The guy at the back of the photo got rejected at his interview, But Graham called him back anyway because he liked the founder, not the idea. Steve Huffman ended up creating Reddit. Then comes the guy with the engineer outfit. His calendar app lasted a month before Google shipped the same thing and killed him. So he auctioned the company on eBay. That stunt is the only reason Graham funded eBay. And the next company became Twitch. These two on the edges went on to fund Airbnb, Stripe, Doordash, Coinbase. 5,000 more came after. The PayPal Mafia built 15 companies. These people built 15 companies and the machine that builds everyone else's. Paul Graham got to back the companies building the future before it was obvious. But to date, the public has had limited access to investing in these companies. USVC gives you access to that. Comment GUIDE and we'll share their investment guide for 2026.",
